744cd2b-88d1-57a5-a1d8-0dcb12bb78fe"] [:db/add "3588ef6d-be33-5b91-9ae2-77a70c5b4721" :answer-field/choices "32399fa1-20c9-5361-9d96-1f602b22d25f"] [:db/add "3588ef6d-be33-5b91-9ae2-77a70c5b4721" :answer-field/choices "cae629d2-0e63-5ef8-b6e5-875bb407408a"] [:db/add "3588ef6d-be33-5b91-9ae2-77a70c5b4721" :answer-field/choices "37aec481-2bc1-550b-93f1-2b0994165854"] [:db/add "3588ef6d-be33-5b91-9ae2-77a70c5b4721" :answer-field/choices "8b45065e-84be-59b1-9c57-ddb9e4cda6f2"] [:db/add "3588ef6d-be33-5b91-9ae2-77a70c5b4721" :answer-field/correct "3744cd2b-88d1-57a5-a1d8-0dcb12bb78fe"] [:db/ensure "3588ef6d-be33-5b91-9ae2-77a70c5b4721" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "596a3028-8196-5628-a399-013186bd1729" :question/id #uuid "596a3028-8196-5628-a399-013186bd1729"] [:db/add "596a3028-8196-5628-a399-013186bd1729" :question/problem "Using the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x - 8 y,\\,v=y,\n$$\n\ncalculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the curve $(x - 8 y)^{2}-(y)=0$ and the line $y=25.$"] [:db/add "596a3028-8196-5628-a399-013186bd1729" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$  \n\nNote that the changes of variables\n\n$$\nu=x - 8 y,\\,v=y\n$$\n\n \n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nSubstituting $x - 8 y=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n(x - 8 y)^{2}-(y)=0\\,⟹\\,u^{2}-v=0\\,⟹\\,v=u^{2}.\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\nv=25.\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}v=u^{2} \\\\ v=25\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,u=\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm 5,25).$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-5\\le u\\le 5,\\,u^{2}\\le v\\le 25\\}.\n$$\n\n![](images/ca/ca54518b097929ecf8756bc699c5fef32de07b174134781e778fdcc395e964fe.png)\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x}&\\frac{∂u}{∂y}\\\\\\frac{∂v}{∂x}&\\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=\\left|\\begin{matrix}1&-8\\\\0&1\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=(1)^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D dxdy &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\iint_Δ |1|\\,dudv \\\\ &=1\\int_{-5}^{5}[\\int_{u^{2}}^{25}dv]du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-5}^{5}[v]_{u^{2}}^{25}du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-5}^{5}(25)-(u^{2})du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-5}^{5}(25 - u^{2})du \\\\ &=1[- \\frac{u^{3}}{3} + 25 u]_{-5}^{5} \\\\ &=1(((125)+(- \\frac{125}{3}))-((-125)+(\\frac{125}{3}))) \\\\ &=1(\\frac{500}{3}) \\\\ &=\\frac{500}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/add "596a3028-8196-5628-a399-013186bd1729" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "596a3028-8196-5628-a399-013186bd1729" :question/answer-fields "3588ef6d-be33-5b91-9ae2-77a70c5b4721"] [:db/ensure "596a3028-8196-5628-a399-013186bd1729" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186129197 :knowledge-point/questions "596a3028-8196-5628-a399-013186bd1729"] [:db/add "fe37c4cf-81b2-5e7d-a4ac-216d9373b83c" :answer/id #uuid "fe37c4cf-81b2-5e7d-a4ac-216d9373b83c"] [:db/add "fe37c4cf-81b2-5e7d-a4ac-216d9373b83c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "fe37c4cf-81b2-5e7d-a4ac-216d9373b83c" :answer/value "288"] [:db/ensure "fe37c4cf-81b2-5e7d-a4ac-216d9373b83c" :answer/validate] [:db/add "72f1279a-9b66-52a1-8b7f-0adc29014b22" :answer/id #uuid "72f1279a-9b66-52a1-8b7f-0adc29014b22"] [:db/add "72f1279a-9b66-52a1-8b7f-0adc29014b22" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "72f1279a-9b66-52a1-8b7f-0adc29014b22" :answer/value "\\frac{256}{3}"] [:db/ensure "72f1279a-9b66-52a1-8b7f-0adc29014b22" :answer/validate] [:db/add "a6911744-3cc0-580b-bfcf-73c927ca18e2" :answer/id #uuid "a6911744-3cc0-580b-bfcf-73c927ca18e2"] [:db/add "a6911744-3cc0-580b-bfcf-73c927ca18e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "a6911744-3cc0-580b-bfcf-73c927ca18e2" :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}"] [:db/ensure "a6911744-3cc0-580b-bfcf-73c927ca18e2" :answer/validate] [:db/add "2c691cbf-d3a7-56be-9269-9915617e50e5" :answer/id #uuid "2c691cbf-d3a7-56be-9269-9915617e50e5"] [:db/add "2c691cbf-d3a7-56be-9269-9915617e50e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "2c691cbf-d3a7-56be-9269-9915617e50e5" :answer/value "\\frac{500}{3}"] [:db/ensure "2c691cbf-d3a7-56be-9269-9915617e50e5" :answer/validate] [:db/add "cd034e13-d7d0-570b-8247-6c28837fa17c" :answer/id #uuid "cd034e13-d7d0-570b-8247-6c28837fa17c"] [:db/add "cd034e13-d7d0-570b-8247-6c28837fa17c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "cd034e13-d7d0-570b-8247-6c28837fa17c" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}"] [:db/ensure "cd034e13-d7d0-570b-8247-6c28837fa17c" :answer/validate] [:db/add "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70" :answer-field/id #uuid "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70"] [:db/add "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70" :answer-field/choices "fe37c4cf-81b2-5e7d-a4ac-216d9373b83c"] [:db/add "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70" :answer-field/choices "72f1279a-9b66-52a1-8b7f-0adc29014b22"] [:db/add "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70" :answer-field/choices "a6911744-3cc0-580b-bfcf-73c927ca18e2"] [:db/add "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70" :answer-field/choices "2c691cbf-d3a7-56be-9269-9915617e50e5"] [:db/add "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70" :answer-field/choices "cd034e13-d7d0-570b-8247-6c28837fa17c"] [:db/add "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70" :answer-field/correct "72f1279a-9b66-52a1-8b7f-0adc29014b22"] [:db/ensure "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "0bbd5512-c745-5506-9589-e476017d1f98" :question/id #uuid "0bbd5512-c745-5506-9589-e476017d1f98"] [:db/add "0bbd5512-c745-5506-9589-e476017d1f98" :question/problem "Using the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x - 6 y,\\,v=y,\n$$\n\ncalculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the curve $(x - 6 y)^{2}-(y)=0$ and the line $y=16.$"] [:db/add "0bbd5512-c745-5506-9589-e476017d1f98" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$  \n\nNote that the changes of variables\n\n$$\nu=x - 6 y,\\,v=y\n$$\n\n \n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nSubstituting $x - 6 y=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n(x - 6 y)^{2}-(y)=0\\,⟹\\,u^{2}-v=0\\,⟹\\,v=u^{2}.\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\nv=16.\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}v=u^{2} \\\\ v=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,u=\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm 4,16).$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-4\\le u\\le 4,\\,u^{2}\\le v\\le 16\\}.\n$$\n\n![](images/38/387e22e062c4ff7f24d26561fe369041f11f59a2b0305f8dc7b3ce49d411031a.png)\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x}&\\frac{∂u}{∂y}\\\\\\frac{∂v}{∂x}&\\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=\\left|\\begin{matrix}1&-6\\\\0&1\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=(1)^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D dxdy &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\iint_Δ |1|\\,dudv \\\\ &=1\\int_{-4}^{4}[\\int_{u^{2}}^{16}dv]du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-4}^{4}[v]_{u^{2}}^{16}du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-4}^{4}(16)-(u^{2})du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-4}^{4}(16 - u^{2})du \\\\ &=1[- \\frac{u^{3}}{3} + 16 u]_{-4}^{4} \\\\ &=1(((64)+(- \\frac{64}{3}))-((-64)+(\\frac{64}{3}))) \\\\ &=1(\\frac{256}{3}) \\\\ &=\\frac{256}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/add "0bbd5512-c745-5506-9589-e476017d1f98" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "0bbd5512-c745-5506-9589-e476017d1f98" :question/answer-fields "55213294-9c90-5c12-b6da-b4a46e8e1b70"] [:db/ensure "0bbd5512-c745-5506-9589-e476017d1f98" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186129197 :knowledge-point/questions "0bbd5512-c745-5506-9589-e476017d1f98"] [:db/add "f915a4c0-c1a0-5652-8118-969be9da31e1" :answer/id #uuid "f915a4c0-c1a0-5652-8118-969be9da31e1"] [:db/add "f915a4c0-c1a0-5652-8118-969be9da31e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "f915a4c0-c1a0-5652-8118-969be9da31e1" :answer/value "36"] [:db/ensure "f915a4c0-c1a0-5652-8118-969be9da31e1" :answer/validate] [:db/add "a8be08e9-1501-58b0-8bd0-b24641111816" :answer/id #uuid "a8be08e9-1501-58b0-8bd0-b24641111816"] [:db/add "a8be08e9-1501-58b0-8bd0-b24641111816" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "a8be08e9-1501-58b0-8bd0-b24641111816" :answer/value "\\frac{256}{3}"] [:db/ensure "a8be08e9-1501-58b0-8bd0-b24641111816" :answer/validate] [:db/add "4731326e-9b9a-5ff6-aff3-587c51ebaef8" :answer/id #uuid "4731326e-9b9a-5ff6-aff3-587c51ebaef8"] [:db/add "4731326e-9b9a-5ff6-aff3-587c51ebaef8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "4731326e-9b9a-5ff6-aff3-587c51ebaef8" :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}"] [:db/ensure "4731326e-9b9a-5ff6-aff3-587c51ebaef8" :answer/validate] [:db/add "1931099c-2d1b-5af8-80f7-090cbab249db" :answer/id #uuid "1931099c-2d1b-5af8-80f7-090cbab249db"] [:db/add "1931099c-2d1b-5af8-80f7-090cbab249db" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "1931099c-2d1b-5af8-80f7-090cbab249db" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}"] [:db/ensure "1931099c-2d1b-5af8-80f7-090cbab249db" :answer/validate] [:db/add "e0af6abf-9221-5426-a3e2-2fa1d2bc4842" :answer/id #uuid "e0af6abf-9221-5426-a3e2-2fa1d2bc4842"] [:db/add "e0af6abf-9221-5426-a3e2-2fa1d2bc4842" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "e0af6abf-9221-5426-a3e2-2fa1d2bc4842" :answer/value "288"] [:db/ensure "e0af6abf-9221-5426-a3e2-2fa1d2bc4842" :answer/validate] [:db/add "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255" :answer-field/id #uuid "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255"] [:db/add "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255" :answer-field/choices "f915a4c0-c1a0-5652-8118-969be9da31e1"] [:db/add "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255" :answer-field/choices "a8be08e9-1501-58b0-8bd0-b24641111816"] [:db/add "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255" :answer-field/choices "4731326e-9b9a-5ff6-aff3-587c51ebaef8"] [:db/add "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255" :answer-field/choices "1931099c-2d1b-5af8-80f7-090cbab249db"] [:db/add "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255" :answer-field/choices "e0af6abf-9221-5426-a3e2-2fa1d2bc4842"] [:db/add "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255" :answer-field/correct "4731326e-9b9a-5ff6-aff3-587c51ebaef8"] [:db/ensure "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "2180d312-6f4f-5d5b-86a4-02dad7f687e5" :question/id #uuid "2180d312-6f4f-5d5b-86a4-02dad7f687e5"] [:db/add "2180d312-6f4f-5d5b-86a4-02dad7f687e5" :question/problem "Using the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x - y,\\,v=y,\n$$\n\ncalculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the curve $(x - y)^{2}-(y)=0$ and the line $y=4.$"] [:db/add "2180d312-6f4f-5d5b-86a4-02dad7f687e5" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$  \n\nNote that the changes of variables\n\n$$\nu=x - y,\\,v=y\n$$\n\n \n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nSubstituting $x - y=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n(x - y)^{2}-(y)=0\\,⟹\\,u^{2}-v=0\\,⟹\\,v=u^{2}.\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\nv=4.\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}v=u^{2} \\\\ v=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,u=\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm 2,4).$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,u^{2}\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\n![](images/b4/b43c84eb76241233dc88e2d6a94bc4e5e24d558f8c9f46a826d0d928059aefc2.png)\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x}&\\frac{∂u}{∂y}\\\\\\frac{∂v}{∂x}&\\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=\\left|\\begin{matrix}1&-1\\\\0&1\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=(1)^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D dxdy &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\iint_Δ |1|\\,dudv \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}[\\int_{u^{2}}^{4}dv]du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}[v]_{u^{2}}^{4}du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}(4)-(u^{2})du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}(4 - u^{2})du \\\\ &=1[- \\frac{u^{3}}{3} + 4 u]_{-2}^{2} \\\\ &=1(((8)+(- \\frac{8}{3}))-((-8)+(\\frac{8}{3}))) \\\\ &=1(\\frac{32}{3}) \\\\ &=\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/add "2180d312-6f4f-5d5b-86a4-02dad7f687e5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "2180d312-6f4f-5d5b-86a4-02dad7f687e5" :question/answer-fields "b54915ac-6f13-58bd-a737-8c93b908a255"] [:db/ensure "2180d312-6f4f-5d5b-86a4-02dad7f687e5" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186129197 :knowledge-point/questions "2180d312-6f4f-5d5b-86a4-02dad7f687e5"] [:db/add "3931285c-aa25-5248-91c8-d02a7c61aa64" :answer/id #uuid "3931285c-aa25-5248-91c8-d02a7c61aa64"] [:db/add "3931285c-aa25-5248-91c8-d02a7c61aa64" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "3931285c-aa25-5248-91c8-d02a7c61aa64" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}"] [:db/ensure "3931285c-aa25-5248-91c8-d02a7c61aa64" :answer/validate] [:db/add "11db1db5-5a0f-5fb0-a754-1b0a0fcb5fb6" :answer/id #uuid "11db1db5-5a0f-5fb0-a754-1b0a0fcb5fb6"] [:db/add "11db1db5-5a0f-5fb0-a754-1b0a0fcb5fb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "11db1db5-5a0f-5fb0-a754-1b0a0fcb5fb6" :answer/value "288"] [:db/ensure "11db1db5-5a0f-5fb0-a754-1b0a0fcb5fb6" :answer/validate] [:db/add "7cbfebff-3fb6-5acc-83eb-383404c2df9f" :answer/id #uuid "7cbfebff-3fb6-5acc-83eb-383404c2df9f"] [:db/add "7cbfebff-3fb6-5acc-83eb-383404c2df9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "7cbfebff-3fb6-5acc-83eb-383404c2df9f" :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}"] [:db/ensure "7cbfebff-3fb6-5acc-83eb-383404c2df9f" :answer/validate] [:db/add "af393de9-3626-52b1-b53c-f870b9f3bd48" :answer/id #uuid "af393de9-3626-52b1-b53c-f870b9f3bd48"] [:db/add "af393de9-3626-52b1-b53c-f870b9f3bd48" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "af393de9-3626-52b1-b53c-f870b9f3bd48" :answer/value "\\frac{256}{3}"] [:db/ensure "af393de9-3626-52b1-b53c-f870b9f3bd48" :answer/validate] [:db/add "c4f2f462-d03e-54dd-8a98-bb5737baebc2" :answer/id #uuid "c4f2f462-d03e-54dd-8a98-bb5737baebc2"] [:db/add "c4f2f462-d03e-54dd-8a98-bb5737baebc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "c4f2f462-d03e-54dd-8a98-bb5737baebc2" :answer/value "\\frac{500}{3}"] [:db/ensure "c4f2f462-d03e-54dd-8a98-bb5737baebc2" :answer/validate] [:db/add "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598" :answer-field/id #uuid "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598"] [:db/add "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598" :answer-field/choices "3931285c-aa25-5248-91c8-d02a7c61aa64"] [:db/add "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598" :answer-field/choices "11db1db5-5a0f-5fb0-a754-1b0a0fcb5fb6"] [:db/add "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598" :answer-field/choices "7cbfebff-3fb6-5acc-83eb-383404c2df9f"] [:db/add "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598" :answer-field/choices "af393de9-3626-52b1-b53c-f870b9f3bd48"] [:db/add "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598" :answer-field/choices "c4f2f462-d03e-54dd-8a98-bb5737baebc2"] [:db/add "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598" :answer-field/correct "11db1db5-5a0f-5fb0-a754-1b0a0fcb5fb6"] [:db/ensure "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "bfbb3e6e-4a50-5fa2-b9fd-b83c3046c21c" :question/id #uuid "bfbb3e6e-4a50-5fa2-b9fd-b83c3046c21c"] [:db/add "bfbb3e6e-4a50-5fa2-b9fd-b83c3046c21c" :question/problem "Using the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x - 8 y,\\,v=y,\n$$\n\ncalculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the curve $(x - 8 y)^{2}-(y)=0$ and the line $y=36.$"] [:db/add "bfbb3e6e-4a50-5fa2-b9fd-b83c3046c21c" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$  \n\nNote that the changes of variables\n\n$$\nu=x - 8 y,\\,v=y\n$$\n\n \n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nSubstituting $x - 8 y=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n(x - 8 y)^{2}-(y)=0\\,⟹\\,u^{2}-v=0\\,⟹\\,v=u^{2}.\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\nv=36.\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}v=u^{2} \\\\ v=36\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,u=\\pm 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm 6,36).$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-6\\le u\\le 6,\\,u^{2}\\le v\\le 36\\}.\n$$\n\n![](images/13/132cec4e3586ef176e2c94e05bbe8860063cce2cef4d0835159da844ea43b8ae.png)\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x}&\\frac{∂u}{∂y}\\\\\\frac{∂v}{∂x}&\\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=\\left|\\begin{matrix}1&-8\\\\0&1\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=(1)^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D dxdy &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\iint_Δ |1|\\,dudv \\\\ &=1\\int_{-6}^{6}[\\int_{u^{2}}^{36}dv]du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-6}^{6}[v]_{u^{2}}^{36}du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-6}^{6}(36)-(u^{2})du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-6}^{6}(36 - u^{2})du \\\\ &=1[- \\frac{u^{3}}{3} + 36 u]_{-6}^{6} \\\\ &=1(((216)+(-72))-((-216)+(72))) \\\\ &=1(288) \\\\ &=288\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/add "bfbb3e6e-4a50-5fa2-b9fd-b83c3046c21c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "bfbb3e6e-4a50-5fa2-b9fd-b83c3046c21c" :question/answer-fields "78c37a21-b63d-5674-9fe8-7c4cc3fd9598"] [:db/ensure "bfbb3e6e-4a50-5fa2-b9fd-b83c3046c21c" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186129197 :knowledge-point/questions "bfbb3e6e-4a50-5fa2-b9fd-b83c3046c21c"] [:db/add "aa93be78-621b-5dba-a958-5824fd7c1535" :answer/id #uuid "aa93be78-621b-5dba-a958-5824fd7c1535"] [:db/add "aa93be78-621b-5dba-a958-5824fd7c1535" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "aa93be78-621b-5dba-a958-5824fd7c1535" :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}"] [:db/ensure "aa93be78-621b-5dba-a958-5824fd7c1535" :answer/validate] [:db/add "419f5596-9ef8-5fd6-9f40-b432bbde2132" :answer/id #uuid "419f5596-9ef8-5fd6-9f40-b432bbde2132"] [:db/add "419f5596-9ef8-5fd6-9f40-b432bbde2132" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "419f5596-9ef8-5fd6-9f40-b432bbde2132" :answer/value "\\frac{256}{3}"] [:db/ensure "419f5596-9ef8-5fd6-9f40-b432bbde2132" :answer/validate] [:db/add "e723eff8-04b7-501d-8051-1b9d4ca4a3fd" :answer/id #uuid "e723eff8-04b7-501d-8051-1b9d4ca4a3fd"] [:db/add "e723eff8-04b7-501d-8051-1b9d4ca4a3fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "e723eff8-04b7-501d-8051-1b9d4ca4a3fd" :answer/value "\\frac{500}{3}"] [:db/ensure "e723eff8-04b7-501d-8051-1b9d4ca4a3fd" :answer/validate] [:db/add "36f2e466-85ea-5119-8556-d5125458bf34" :answer/id #uuid "36f2e466-85ea-5119-8556-d5125458bf34"] [:db/add "36f2e466-85ea-5119-8556-d5125458bf34" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "36f2e466-85ea-5119-8556-d5125458bf34" :answer/value "36"] [:db/ensure "36f2e466-85ea-5119-8556-d5125458bf34" :answer/validate] [:db/add "d474f446-afd7-5635-942c-718b8fb2cb61" :answer/id #uuid "d474f446-afd7-5635-942c-718b8fb2cb61"] [:db/add "d474f446-afd7-5635-942c-718b8fb2cb61" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "d474f446-afd7-5635-942c-718b8fb2cb61" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}"] [:db/ensure "d474f446-afd7-5635-942c-718b8fb2cb61" :answer/validate] [:db/add "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4" :answer-field/id #uuid "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4"] [:db/add "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4" :answer-field/choices "aa93be78-621b-5dba-a958-5824fd7c1535"] [:db/add "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4" :answer-field/choices "419f5596-9ef8-5fd6-9f40-b432bbde2132"] [:db/add "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4" :answer-field/choices "e723eff8-04b7-501d-8051-1b9d4ca4a3fd"] [:db/add "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4" :answer-field/choices "36f2e466-85ea-5119-8556-d5125458bf34"] [:db/add "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4" :answer-field/choices "d474f446-afd7-5635-942c-718b8fb2cb61"] [:db/add "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4" :answer-field/correct "aa93be78-621b-5dba-a958-5824fd7c1535"] [:db/ensure "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "ec1bbf79-9916-53c6-8b93-5585f4221005" :question/id #uuid "ec1bbf79-9916-53c6-8b93-5585f4221005"] [:db/add "ec1bbf79-9916-53c6-8b93-5585f4221005" :question/problem "Using the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x - 8 y,\\,v=y,\n$$\n\ncalculate the area of the finite region $D$ bounded by the curve $(x - 8 y)^{2}-(y)=0$ and the line $y=4.$"] [:db/add "ec1bbf79-9916-53c6-8b93-5585f4221005" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$  \n\nNote that the changes of variables\n\n$$\nu=x - 8 y,\\,v=y\n$$\n\n \n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nSubstituting $x - 8 y=u$ and $y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n(x - 8 y)^{2}-(y)=0\\,⟹\\,u^{2}-v=0\\,⟹\\,v=u^{2}.\n$$\n\nwhile substituting $y=v$ into the equation of the second curve, we obtain\n\n$$\nv=4.\n$$\n\nTo find the intersections of the curves in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}v=u^{2} \\\\ v=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,u=\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm 2,4).$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,u^{2}\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\n![](images/b4/b43c84eb76241233dc88e2d6a94bc4e5e24d558f8c9f46a826d0d928059aefc2.png)\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x}&\\frac{∂u}{∂y}\\\\\\frac{∂v}{∂x}&\\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=\\left|\\begin{matrix}1&-8\\\\0&1\\end{matrix}\\right| \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=(1)^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D dxdy &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\iint_Δ |1|\\,dudv \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}[\\int_{u^{2}}^{4}dv]du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}[v]_{u^{2}}^{4}du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}(4)-(u^{2})du \\\\ &=1\\int_{-2}^{2}(4 - u^{2})du \\\\ &=1[- \\frac{u^{3}}{3} + 4 u]_{-2}^{2} \\\\ &=1(((8)+(- \\frac{8}{3}))-((-8)+(\\frac{8}{3}))) \\\\ &=1(\\frac{32}{3}) \\\\ &=\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/add "ec1bbf79-9916-53c6-8b93-5585f4221005" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "ec1bbf79-9916-53c6-8b93-5585f4221005" :question/answer-fields "04a58d4d-d91f-5e80-8080-2159132921d4"] [:db/ensure "ec1bbf79-9916-53c6-8b93-5585f4221005" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186129197 :knowledge-point/questions "ec1bbf79-9916-53c6-8b93-5585f4221005"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "947b491b-e0cd-53f3-9e2e-36be4cf5446a"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/script "generators/bd/bd1955c8d0b26b370c54ff3d7d8c2e3b3d540dfcfbd64f33b5bc02453de35fce/17592186129197.py"] [:db/add 17592186129197 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] [:db/ensure 17592186129197 :knowledge-point/validate]]
